35,2,1,talk,May,,The late-evening pilot actually hit its cost target. And the accessibility lifts finished on time. We have proof these work.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""May"",""self"":true,""raw"":""May: The late-evening pilot actually hit its cost target. And the accessibility lifts finished on time. We have proof these work.""}]}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The roster books are grim. Overtime is masking a structural collapse. We cannot promise night extensions without bodies to run them.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The audits show most lost time is waiting for connections, not paying. Mid-city runs are slower, but platforms clear at the old rate.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The minutes show the ferry and rail offices never agreed on data terms. The pre-war shells hide voids that stop work for weeks.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ledger shows a ring-fenced grant balance, but operating subsidies are trimmed. Ticketing fees now exceed our resurfacing budget. We are paying for the past, not the future.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, the pilot proves the model works, but you’re right that staffing is the bottleneck. We can’t just copy the timetable without the crew.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, exactly. The pilot proves demand, not supply. We are borrowing from the future to cover tonight’s gaps.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, the data confirms my suspicion. We are fixing the wrong part of the trip. The bottleneck is connection waiting, not ticketing.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, the data is clear. But @Benjamin, the voids in the shells mean any station work will stall. We must trust the ground first.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the data aligns with my ledger findings. We are bleeding money on ticketing fees while the actual time loss is in waiting.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shizue, the accessibility records show those lifts actually finished on time. The ground didn’t hide voids there, so maybe we can trust that specific delivery date.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shizue, the maintenance contract has spare capacity for lifts. That specific risk is mitigated, unlike the crew shortage.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that spare capacity is a relief. It means we can fix the connection delays without the staffing nightmare you described.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I am glad the lift crews are ready. It eases my worry about the ground. Let us see if the rest holds.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the spare lift capacity is a quiet win. It lets us fix the real delays without the staffing crisis you warned about.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,"So, the lifts work, the night pilot paid off, but the crews are gone. We need a plan that doesn’t require a miracle workforce.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Agreed. We need a plan that fits the bodies we actually have, not the ones we wish for.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"Exactly. We must target the connection waits, not the ticket queues. That is where the real time is lost.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Midori"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Midori: Exactly. We must target the connection waits, not the ticket queues. That is where the real time is lost.""}]}"
53,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I am relieved the lift crews are ready. It eases my worry about the ground. Let us see if the rest holds.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. We must stop funding the ticketing bleed and focus on the connection delays where the real time is lost.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
