60,3,1,talk,May,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,The night extension is a fantasy without the crew. The fare platform ignores the real time loss. I’m leaning toward the bus corridor.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Midori,,"The data points to connection waits, not ticketing. The bus corridor fixes mid-city speed, but I worry it ignores the platform bottlenecks.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"The pre-war shells hide voids, so station work is risky. The bus corridor avoids that ground risk. I am leaning toward the bus corridor.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ledger shows ticketing fees are a drain, not a solution. The bus corridor avoids the staffing crisis and the ground risks. I am leaning toward the bus corridor.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"The pilots prove the night model works, but Benjamin is right about the crew. I’m leaning toward the bus corridor to fix the mid-city speed without the staffing nightmare.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, precisely. The corridor uses existing assets, not phantom staff. It is the only option that respects the roster books.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I agree the corridor respects the roster. But does it actually cut the connection waiting time my audits flagged?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, the corridor speeds up the mid-city runs, which should help clear the platforms faster. It avoids the hidden ground risks I fear.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the corridor reduces mid-city travel time, which should ease the connection pressure. It is the only option that fits our current reality.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,"@Midori, it tightens the mid-city loop, which should help connections. Plus, the old lane-priority stretches failed, so this dedicated design is a real improvement.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, it doesn’t eliminate waiting, but it makes the ride faster. That’s the only lever we actually have left.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@May, the dedicated lanes address the speed loss I measured. It is the best fit for the data we have.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I am glad the data supports this. The corridor avoids the hidden voids in the old shells. It feels like the safest path forward for us.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the ledger confirms the ticketing drain. The corridor is the only path that respects our actual constraints and avoids the staffing crisis.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,May,,I’m voting for the bus corridor. It respects the crew limits and fixes the speed loss we actually measured. Let’s move forward.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am voting for the bus corridor. It is the only plan that does not require hiring ghosts. Let us proceed.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I am voting for the bus corridor. It targets the speed loss my audits confirmed, without demanding impossible staffing.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I am voting for the bus corridor. It avoids the hidden ground risks and respects our current limits. A steady, safe choice.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I am voting for the bus corridor. It respects the ledger’s limits and avoids the staffing crisis. A quiet, sensible choice.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
